The Online Game Database Management System is a relational database project designed to manage game-related data such as player accounts, characters, regions, items, creeps (monsters), and encounters.

This system demonstrates the implementation of:
            Entity tables
            Weak entities
            Relationship tables
            Primary and Foreign Keys
            One-to-Many and Many-to-Many relationships

 Database Entities:
1️. Account
      - Stores player account details.
      - AcctName (Primary Key)
      - Password
      - Subscriber details
      - Account creation date
2️. Character
       - Stores player characters.
       - Linked to Account
       -    Linked to Region
       Stores level, experience, health, mana
3️. Region
      Stores region/environment details.
      Climate
      Precipitation
      Foliage
4️. Item
     Stores item types.
     Item name
     Item type (Weapon, Armor, etc.)
     Item damage
5️. ItemInstantiation
     Represents items owned by characters.
6️. Creep
     Stores monster details.
7️. CreepInstantiation
     Represents creeps appearing in regions.
8️. RanInto
     Many-to-Many relationship between Character and CreepInstantiation.

 Relationships:

        - One Account → Many Characters
        - One Region → Many Characters
        - One Character → Many Items
        - One Item → Many ItemInstances
        - One Creep → Many CreepInstances
        - Many Characters ↔ Many CreepInstances

 Technologies Used:
           . MySQL
           . SQL (DDL, DML)
           . ER Diagram Design
           . Relational Schema Mapping

 Concepts Implemented:

           . Primary Keys
           . Foreign Keys
           . Weak Entities
           . Many-to-Many Relationships
           . Composite Primary Keys
           . Normalization

 How to Run:

           . Create the database in MySQL.
           . Execute all CREATE TABLE statements.
           . Insert sample values.
           .  Run SELECT queries to test relationships.


